{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "את מחתות החטאים האלה בנפשותם", :translit "et machtot ha-chata'im ha-eleh b'nafshotam", :gloss "the fire-pans of the sinners these at the cost of their lives"} {:he "בחנפי לעגי מעוג חרק עלי שנימו", :translit "b'chanafi la'agei mo'ug charak alav shinav", :gloss "the hypocrites mock at cakes he gnashes at him his teeth"} {:he "חרק", :translit "charak", :gloss "he gnashed"} {:he "קרח", :translit "korach", :gloss "Korah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "חרק", :b "קרח"}], :frame {:text "The phrase בחנפי לעגי מעוג חרק עלי שנימו appears in Job, and Resh Lakish interprets it as referring to Korah's followers: Korah flattered them with food and drink, provoking the prince of Gehinnom to gnash his teeth at them. The equation of חרק and קרח by gematria links the verse's language directly to Korah.", :sources ["Job 34:30 (per the rendering)" "Numbers Rabbah 18:18"]}} {:quotes [{:he "החטאים האלה בנפשותם", :translit "ha-chata'im ha-eleh b'nafshotam", :gloss "the sinners these at the cost of their lives"} {:he "את החטאים את עמלק", :translit "et ha-chata'im et amalek", :gloss "the sinners Amalek"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["החטאים האלה בנפשותם" "את החטאים את עמלק"]}], :frame {:text "The shared phrase החטאים links Korah's congregation to Amalek: just as Korah's men sinned at the cost of their lives, Amalek sinned at the cost of his life, for though he saw all the wonders done for Israel he still engaged them. The parable of one who saw a boiling bath and jumped into it is cited in Midrash Mishle regarding Amalek's recklessness.", :sources ["Midrash Mishle (as cited by Ba'al HaTurim)"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "חרק", :a-value 308, :b "קרח", :b-value 308, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["החטאים האלה בנפשותם" "את החטאים את עמלק"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "החטאים האלה בנפשותם", :refs ["Numbers 17:3"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensiti